      ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\tan x?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer.\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The domain is all real numbers except $x=\\frac{\\pi}{2}+n\\pi.$\n- **II.** The function is positive throughout $(-\\frac{\\pi}{2}+n\\pi,n\\pi).$\n- **III.** The least positive period is $\\frac{\\pi}{2}.$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "50e6a951-f54e-50fb-a329-6d231b56a184",
          ":answer-field/key": "I",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "47b01152-b0f2-5ae6-9d6d-4a2719d16142",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "false"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "6e65aea4-d95d-50c5-b510-e406a454cb33",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "true"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "6e65aea4-d95d-50c5-b510-e406a454cb33"
          ]
        },
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "30c2fb0b-e997-5ff4-b8c8-2415dbb85135",
          ":answer-field/key": "II",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "23168dfc-28ab-5998-8fb2-aba59f91f809",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "false"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "78836344-90d2-59c0-9fa4-cbfbc31d548a",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "true"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "23168dfc-28ab-5998-8fb2-aba59f91f809"
          ]
        },
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "48690848-ab68-59a8-818b-e95b027ddc1a",
          ":answer-field/key": "III",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "d691da8e-b1bf-5a45-8257-9ce8303588c3",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "false"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "ae3ecf10-e077-553c-b1ea-a6842ea40238",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "true"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "d691da8e-b1bf-5a45-8257-9ce8303588c3"
          ]
        }
      ],
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\tan x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186176049/tangent.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true. The function is defined everywhere except where $x=\\frac{\\pi}{2}+n\\pi.$\n\n- Statement II is false. The function is positive on $(0,\\frac{\\pi}{2})$ and negative on $(-\\frac{\\pi}{2},0).$ The period is $\\pi,$ so these signs repeat after each integer multiple of $\\pi.$\n\n- Statement III is false. The graph repeats after a horizontal shift of $\\pi,$ and no smaller positive shift repeats the whole graph. Therefore, the least positive period is $\\pi.$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I only\"."
    },
